Source: sherpa-onnx
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Grigory Tuboltsev <gtubolcev@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cmake, libonnxruntime-dev, patchelf
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: sherpa-onnx
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: pulseaudio-utils | alsa-utils
Description: local speech recognition and synthesis (sherpa-onnx)
 sherpa-onnx runs speech models with ONNX Runtime on the CPU:
 text to speech (VITS/Piper, Matcha, Kokoro, Kitten, Pocket TTS,
 Supertonic, ZipVoice), speech recognition, VAD, speaker diarization.
 Models: https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx/releases
 .
 This package has the command line tools, sherpa-say (speaks a text with
 a model directory) and the C and C++ API libraries.

Package: libsherpa-onnx-dev
Architecture: amd64
Section: libdevel
Depends: sherpa-onnx (= ${binary:Version}), libonnxruntime-dev, ${misc:Depends}
Description: local speech recognition and synthesis (sherpa-onnx) - headers
 sherpa-onnx runs speech models with ONNX Runtime on the CPU.
 .
 This package has the headers of the C and C++ API and sherpa-onnx.pc.
